WEBVTT

00:02.369 --> 00:03.836
Legend has it that...

00:05.005 --> 00:07.803
...during the Heian Period, there were
men who fought with no weapons...

00:08.141 --> 00:13.477
They were known as the Men of
Carnage and they reigned undefeated.

00:14.948 --> 00:20.113
Their technique was called
the Mutsu Enmei Style.

00:33.233 --> 00:40.662
<i>The Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

00:40.941 --> 00:46.777
<i>Rushing through my innocent</i>
<i>youth without a care in the world.</i>

00:48.315 --> 00:54.220
<i>This soul of mine is</i>
<i>so easy to influence.</i>

00:55.889 --> 00:59.655
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

00:59.759 --> 01:02.956
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

01:06.733 --> 01:13.798
<i>This is what I'm wishing</i>
<i>for as I sing this song.</i>

01:13.974 --> 01:19.810
<i>I want you to acknowledge</i>
<i>me, that's all.</i>

01:20.680 --> 01:27.950
<i>You smiled at me for</i>
<i>the very first time.</i>

01:28.121 --> 01:36.529
<i>Thank you so much, thank you</i>
<i>from the bottom of my heart.</i>

01:37.230 --> 01:38.891
<i>I'll never forget it.</i>

01:48.642 --> 01:52.078
<i>The Age of Chaos</i>
<i>Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

01:52.812 --> 01:57.181
<i>Year 1866</i>
<i>Second Year of Kei-ou</i>

01:59.085 --> 02:05.183
<i>Teradaya</i>

02:05.559 --> 02:08.119
Eight years have passed...

02:08.295 --> 02:12.197
...since Ryoma Sakamoto and
Izumi Mutsu parted ways in Edo...

02:12.799 --> 02:17.236
The currents of history are now
flowing at a torrential pace...

02:17.437 --> 02:20.770
...and Ryoma is right
in the midst of it all...

02:22.542 --> 02:27.206
That's right, Miyoshi, the Satsuma-
Choshu Alliance was sealed yesterday!

02:27.347 --> 02:30.646
It's a great achievement, and
it's all thanks to your efforts!

02:30.750 --> 02:32.843
Hey, don't give me all the credit.

02:33.420 --> 02:37.789
Either the Bakufu will be destroyed,
or Japan will be destroyed...

02:39.826 --> 02:41.157
...simple as that!

02:43.964 --> 02:49.869
Choshu's Katsura and Satsuma's Saigo,
they deserve a lot of the credit, too.

02:50.003 --> 02:53.404
At any rate, the Choshu
clan has been saved...

02:53.540 --> 02:57.067
Actually, the way has been
paved for the entire nation!

02:57.877 --> 02:59.674
Now we can overthrow the Shogunate!

03:01.815 --> 03:04.943
By the way, Lord Sakamoto,
please be careful.

03:05.685 --> 03:09.314
Don't forget, you're now Ryoma
Sakamoto the national hero.

03:09.623 --> 03:12.057
I've heard that both
the Fushimi Police Squad...

03:12.192 --> 03:15.389
...and the Shinsengumi have
listed you as a target.

03:15.528 --> 03:17.758
Cha, cha, cha! If it comes to that...

03:17.864 --> 03:21.322
I'll just use this thing
Takasugi gave me, to scare them...

03:22.202 --> 03:23.794
...and run for my life!

03:24.304 --> 03:29.003
<i>Shinsengumi</i>

03:46.226 --> 03:47.124
I see...

03:47.227 --> 03:49.593
Actually, would you mind
me asking you something?

03:49.729 --> 03:50.354
Sure.

03:51.331 --> 03:55.267
You have been conferred mastership
of the Hokushin Itto Style.

03:55.769 --> 03:59.603
So, why are you carrying
around a pistol like that?

04:00.273 --> 04:01.331
Because I lost once.

04:06.379 --> 04:09.576
A long time ago, I lost to someone.

04:25.565 --> 04:26.463
What the...

04:39.913 --> 04:45.374
For the first time in my life, I was
motivated to go for the kill, and then...

04:46.853 --> 04:48.013
...I lost.

04:48.755 --> 04:52.247
Now that I'm what they call an
anti-Shogunate Imperialist...

04:52.392 --> 04:54.326
...all I do is think
about the future of Japan.

04:54.427 --> 04:58.090
But I'm just an ex-swordsman, and
a lot of it's way over my head.

04:58.565 --> 05:00.863
I always thought that I'd
make my living as a swordsman...

05:01.000 --> 05:04.197
...but ever since I lost to
that man, I've changed my mind.

05:04.437 --> 05:07.634
You mean, you think a
pistol's better than a sword?

05:07.774 --> 05:08.763
No.

05:09.409 --> 05:12.572
I just decided to go
after my dream, that's all.

05:13.313 --> 05:16.476
The reason I'm working for the
future of the country is, well...

05:16.816 --> 05:19.046
...it's partly because it'll
bring me closer to my dream.

05:19.252 --> 05:20.310
Right...

05:20.487 --> 05:22.648
...and what does that have
to do with packing a pistol?

05:23.089 --> 05:23.748
Huh?

05:23.923 --> 05:26.585
I'll be damned, what were
we talking about, again?

05:27.660 --> 05:30.322
The thing is, I can't
bring myself to kill.

05:30.530 --> 05:34.125
If my opponent's a samurai, he's not
going to run away if I draw my sword.

05:34.768 --> 05:38.727
But even a samurai would back
off if I were to fire a pistol.

05:39.239 --> 05:40.763
Then I could make my escape.

05:41.207 --> 05:45.143
I'm a man who gave up his sword.
Since the day I lost to that fellow...

05:45.245 --> 05:46.678
So it's perfect for me!

05:46.946 --> 05:47.708
Bang!

06:14.707 --> 06:16.402
Lord Sakamoto! You are in danger!

06:16.843 --> 06:19.004
The Shogunate's men
have surrounded us!

06:19.312 --> 06:20.336
O-Ryo.

06:20.480 --> 06:23.074
Calm down and go put on
some clothes, will you?

06:23.483 --> 06:24.973
Miyoshi doesn't know where to look!

06:30.023 --> 06:31.217
I was just...

06:32.625 --> 06:34.388
Lord Sakamoto! There's no time to lose!

06:36.396 --> 06:38.455
Miyoshi, don't jump the gun now.

06:38.832 --> 06:39.594
Right.

06:43.269 --> 06:46.898
Let's just stay cool and
get the hell out of here!

06:48.241 --> 06:49.606
Lord Sakamoto!

06:54.247 --> 06:56.374
You're Ryo Sakamoto, aren't you?

06:56.482 --> 06:59.349
You are under arrest for disturbing the
peace of the nation as a lawless ronin...

06:59.919 --> 07:03.218
...by decree of the Fushimi
Magistrate, Lord Higo no Kami.

07:03.389 --> 07:04.651
We advise you not to resist!

07:09.963 --> 07:11.692
Better get out of the way.

07:11.831 --> 07:13.765
If I hit you, you'll die...

07:21.274 --> 07:24.266
Lord Sakamoto! At least try to hit them!

07:24.377 --> 07:25.810
But they'll die if I do that.

07:26.246 --> 07:29.010
And if you don't hit them,
we'll be the ones to die.

07:32.385 --> 07:33.113
Whoops.

07:33.586 --> 07:35.019
Am I out of bullets already?

07:35.154 --> 07:36.178
Lord Sakamoto!

07:36.289 --> 07:39.952
Uh, now where did I put my bullets?

07:40.293 --> 07:41.783
Now! Get him!

08:09.555 --> 08:11.989
Oh, so there was another bullet left.

08:12.992 --> 08:14.186
Now's our chance.

08:14.294 --> 08:14.885
Miyoshi!

08:15.695 --> 08:16.627
Let's get out of here!

08:16.896 --> 08:17.954
Lord Sakamoto!

08:19.499 --> 08:20.523
After them!

08:20.633 --> 08:21.327
Right!

08:24.470 --> 08:25.402
Miyoshi...

08:25.772 --> 08:26.534
Yes.

08:32.979 --> 08:34.173
We'll go after Sakamoto!

08:34.347 --> 08:35.075
All right!

08:37.984 --> 08:38.882
What happened?

08:40.820 --> 08:42.685
They split up, and got away.

08:43.389 --> 08:44.253
However...

08:44.791 --> 08:46.452
...we did manage to wound him.

08:46.559 --> 08:48.459
So? How many men did we lose?

08:48.594 --> 08:50.027
Actually, none...

08:50.129 --> 08:53.895
We didn't lose a single man, because
Sakamoto never even drew his sword!

08:54.000 --> 08:57.663
But Sakamoto's a
Master of the Hokushin Itto-Style.

08:57.837 --> 08:58.769
Right...

08:59.238 --> 09:00.728
Do you think maybe he's
an idiot or something?

09:01.040 --> 09:02.302
Don't ask me!

09:05.745 --> 09:08.373
Please be safe, Lord Sakamoto.

09:51.090 --> 09:53.718
I wonder if Miyoshi
was able to get away?

09:55.528 --> 09:58.520
This isn't good, the
bleeding won't stop...

09:59.966 --> 10:03.163
I can feel my strength
draining away, bit by bit...

10:10.843 --> 10:13.869
This is really bad...

10:20.019 --> 10:22.817
Am I surrounded?

10:30.930 --> 10:33.956
We heard that the Fushimi
Police Squad was on the move...

10:34.167 --> 10:35.634
...so we decided to come out...

10:36.302 --> 10:40.238
And look what we've
stumbled upon. The big prize!

10:41.107 --> 10:44.702
Ryoma Sakamoto, the
Shinsengumi is here to...

10:45.945 --> 10:47.310
...claim your head!

10:48.481 --> 10:49.778
Hmm?

10:50.083 --> 10:52.881
Not the reunion you
imagined, is it, Sakamoto?

10:53.019 --> 10:54.418
Cha, cha, cha...

10:54.787 --> 10:57.688
So you're Deputy
Commander Hijikata of that...

10:57.790 --> 11:01.988
...terrifying band of
assassins, the Shinsengumi?

11:03.563 --> 11:05.588
Soushi, kill him!

11:06.666 --> 11:11.535
There's no pride to be had in
killing a wounded Ryoma Sakamoto.

11:11.838 --> 11:13.772
You haven't changed at all, Soushi...

11:13.906 --> 11:15.669
But never mind.

11:15.875 --> 11:18.844
Anyone can kill Sakamoto
in his current state!

11:19.212 --> 11:19.803
Go for it!

11:25.051 --> 11:28.509
Really, it looks
like I'm in for it now...

11:29.355 --> 11:30.720
Not necessarily!

11:37.663 --> 11:40.530
Ryoma, you haven't changed at all...

11:41.033 --> 11:44.969
If you would just go for it, you could
get out of this mess without a scratch.

11:45.204 --> 11:48.833
But you can't bring yourself
to kill. You're way too gentle!

11:49.876 --> 11:51.309
Izumi!

11:56.649 --> 11:59.618
Cha, cha, cha! It's good to see you!

11:59.752 --> 12:02.346
It's been seven, no, eight years now.

12:02.455 --> 12:04.082
You're still the same old Izumi!

12:04.223 --> 12:05.815
Hey, same goes for you, too.

12:06.292 --> 12:09.728
So, did you ever get your Kurofune?

12:10.329 --> 12:12.229
Well, I'm working on it.

12:12.365 --> 12:15.357
I started a trading company
called Kaientai in Nagasaki.

12:15.535 --> 12:19.528
I'll be able to set out and see the
world once the nation's under control.

12:23.075 --> 12:24.064
Hey, by the way...

12:24.410 --> 12:25.104
Hmm?

12:31.450 --> 12:32.348
Bastard!

12:40.393 --> 12:42.293
You better watch out!

12:42.695 --> 12:45.664
Hey, you should've told me that first.

13:06.652 --> 13:08.142
He's powerful!

13:08.287 --> 13:09.584
Who the hell is this guy?

13:09.722 --> 13:10.780
Step back.

13:11.424 --> 13:13.085
This man is way out of your league.

13:13.292 --> 13:14.384
Deputy!

13:15.494 --> 13:18.122
Do you remember what
I told you that day?

13:20.233 --> 13:24.226
"In the future, if I ever
find you standing in my way..."

13:24.704 --> 13:28.162
"...then I'll kill you myself!"

13:29.508 --> 13:30.907
I hope you remember that.

13:34.880 --> 13:38.111
Hijikata, that man is mine.

13:38.918 --> 13:41.478
Remember, I claimed him first.

13:41.687 --> 13:43.086
Soushi...

14:14.920 --> 14:18.083
Hijikata, that man is mine.

14:19.125 --> 14:21.525
Remember, I claimed him first.

14:21.827 --> 14:23.124
Soushi...

14:29.935 --> 14:35.373
It's been eight years since
I first met you in Edo...

14:37.943 --> 14:41.435
Tennen Rishin Style, Soushi Okita...

14:42.782 --> 14:46.047
If you dare mock me any
further, I'll kill you!

14:47.453 --> 14:52.015
At your current level, you have
no chance against Ryoma or me!

14:59.398 --> 15:03.391
When he dodged your first thrust,
he kicked you in the scabbard.

15:16.549 --> 15:17.379
What?

15:17.616 --> 15:20.346
Had he been serious,
you'd be dead now.

15:25.324 --> 15:28.418
This time, I want you
to go all-out with me.

15:40.339 --> 15:42.330
Sure, but...

15:42.475 --> 15:44.443
We're going to have to
settle this another day.

15:44.777 --> 15:45.641
What?

15:46.145 --> 15:49.114
Because right now, I
really don't have the time.

15:56.155 --> 15:59.249
Ryoma, let's go.

16:04.663 --> 16:05.721
Wait!

16:09.502 --> 16:10.662
Hijikata!

16:11.971 --> 16:13.962
I have something to say to you, too.

16:15.107 --> 16:19.942
In the future, if I ever catch you
laying a hand on a friend of mine...

16:20.613 --> 16:25.516
...then I'll take that dream of yours, the
Shinsengumi, and smash it to pieces!

16:26.185 --> 16:27.345
I'll remember that!

16:28.220 --> 16:29.847
Another time, Okita!

16:34.393 --> 16:35.291
Come back here!

16:35.428 --> 16:36.326
Don't go after them!

16:37.430 --> 16:38.897
But Deputy Commander...

16:39.265 --> 16:40.596
It's no use.

16:40.966 --> 16:43.867
At any rate, this is something we should
leave to the Fushimi Police Squad...

16:44.303 --> 16:46.771
It's not the Shinsengumi's job.

16:47.373 --> 16:48.567
Let's go!

16:53.045 --> 16:53.909
Soushi!

16:55.581 --> 16:56.570
Yes.

17:02.488 --> 17:04.080
Damn him...

17:04.457 --> 17:08.951
Calling the Shinsengumi my dream!

17:09.295 --> 17:10.728
Well, he's right!

17:11.096 --> 17:14.361
Together, Kondoh and I will
make the Shinsengumi great.

17:14.800 --> 17:16.461
That's my dream.

17:16.702 --> 17:18.795
And no one's going to stand in my way!

17:26.212 --> 17:27.406
Hey, Izumi...

17:27.546 --> 17:31.539
I should tell you, there's a
man named Mutsu in the Kaientai...

17:31.684 --> 17:34.152
Don't talk, pal. It's
not good for your wound.

17:34.286 --> 17:36.754
His real name is Kojiro Date, but...

17:36.889 --> 17:38.880
...when I told him about you...

17:38.991 --> 17:43.155
...he decided to change
his name to Younosuke Mutsu.

17:43.696 --> 17:47.427
I guess I must've sounded nostalgic
when I was talking about you...

17:47.566 --> 17:50.057
If that doesn't sit well with you,
I'll tell him to change his name back...

17:50.202 --> 17:52.033
...but are you okay with it, Izumi?

17:52.338 --> 17:53.362
Sure, I don't mind.

17:54.707 --> 17:57.540
But listen, where
should I take you now?

17:57.776 --> 17:58.970
Oh, hey, sorry!

17:59.211 --> 18:02.146
The Satsuma residence in Fushimi...

18:08.387 --> 18:11.356
<i>Satsuma</i>

18:11.524 --> 18:12.821
Have Lord Saigo receive them!

18:12.925 --> 18:13.550
Right away, sir!

18:13.659 --> 18:14.421
Summon the doctor!

18:14.527 --> 18:17.018
I'll get a futon right away!

18:18.330 --> 18:19.888
Hey, Sakamoto!

18:22.234 --> 18:23.895
Tell me, are you all right?

18:24.537 --> 18:26.505
Oh, man, you got cut!

18:30.876 --> 18:34.368
When Miyoshi got here,
he was cut up pretty bad...

18:35.381 --> 18:37.975
When I heard that you'd
been attacked, I feared...

18:38.183 --> 18:40.743
Sorry to make you worry, Saigo.

18:41.720 --> 18:43.984
Hey, is the doctor here yet?

18:44.123 --> 18:45.488
Where's the doctor?

18:49.962 --> 18:53.989
By the way, Sakamoto, that man
who carried you here on his back...

18:54.900 --> 18:56.561
...who is he, anyway?

19:00.372 --> 19:02.840
Is he a comrade of yours, Sakamoto?

19:03.042 --> 19:04.304
Not a comrade...

19:06.612 --> 19:09.308
That guy, he's a...

19:10.382 --> 19:12.282
He's a friend of mine.

19:24.563 --> 19:26.087
You're pretty good at that, aren't you?

19:30.169 --> 19:31.466
Hanjiro...

19:32.271 --> 19:34.933
Tell me, what's your name?

19:37.776 --> 19:39.209
Izumi Mutsu.

19:39.578 --> 19:42.172
My name is Hanjiro Nakamura.

19:42.514 --> 19:43.879
I know that.

19:44.450 --> 19:49.387
You're a master of the Jigen Style, a
man who'd give his life for Satsuma...

19:49.588 --> 19:51.613
...no, actually for Saigo.

19:52.024 --> 19:56.085
If you know that much about me,
then I have nothing more to say.

20:02.835 --> 20:03.927
This way!

20:07.072 --> 20:08.767
Let me take a look.

20:09.541 --> 20:11.065
This is quite serious.

20:11.276 --> 20:15.269
Hey, you need to be more
gentle with me, or it'll hurt!

20:15.781 --> 20:17.078
You must bear with me.

20:17.216 --> 20:19.946
If we don't stop the bleeding,
your life will be in danger.

20:21.954 --> 20:23.819
More importantly, Sakamoto...

20:23.989 --> 20:27.254
You're going to have to take
better care of yourself from now on...

20:28.160 --> 20:31.288
Without you, we'll never
achieve our goals for the nation.

20:31.430 --> 20:32.897
Cha, cha, cha!

20:32.965 --> 20:34.557
Whether you live or you die...

20:35.901 --> 20:38.631
That doesn't really matter, you know.

20:38.904 --> 20:42.806
I'm not going to stop
going off on my own...

20:43.142 --> 20:44.700
Sakamoto...

20:44.810 --> 20:49.008
Now, all I need to think about is whether
we can achieve our goals or not.

20:49.148 --> 20:53.778
If I die then it was
meant to be, Saigo!

20:55.688 --> 21:01.718
Anyway, for someone to kill me now,
they'd need an army of at least 100 men!

21:02.027 --> 21:04.222
And why is that?

21:07.966 --> 21:10.662
Because my friend is nearby...

21:13.405 --> 21:15.999
But this pain...

21:16.141 --> 21:21.101
<i>To be continued...</i>

21:32.257 --> 21:44.294
<i>Those summer stars, I looked up at</i>
<i>them alone when I was a troubled child.</i>

21:44.570 --> 21:54.309
<i>My loneliness and the vast night</i>
<i>sky, melting and shining in eternity.</i>

21:54.446 --> 22:03.445
<i>I just don't know what this</i>
<i>dream means, if it leads to love...</i>

22:03.589 --> 22:14.261
<i>Even if it's just "hello,"</i>
<i>I want to hear your voice.</i>

22:15.300 --> 22:21.432
<i>The person I am today</i>
<i>is about to disappear...</i>

22:21.807 --> 22:24.799
<i>What is it that will hold me back?</i>

22:25.677 --> 22:31.946
<i>Will it be you? I won't ask you now.</i>

22:32.251 --> 22:37.746
<i>Maybe if we ever meet again...</i>

22:52.538 --> 22:54.335
The Satsuma-Choshu
Alliance has been sealed.

22:54.439 --> 22:57.101
Are you going to give Shinsaku
Takasugi a hand next, Ryoma?

22:57.242 --> 22:59.836
All of this will help you get
closer to realizing your dream.

23:00.445 --> 23:02.413
Next episode of the Age of Chaos...

23:02.548 --> 23:04.015
<i>The Dragon Incarnate</i>

23:04.149 --> 23:06.310
Pay close attention, and wait!
